      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ حَرَّمَ رَسُولُ اَللَّهِ صَلَّى اَللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ اَلْمَدِينَةَ فَقَالَ «نَعَمْ حَرَّمَ بَرِيداً فِي بَرِيدٍ عِضَاهاً» قُلْتُ صَيْدَهَا قَالَ «لاَ يَكْذِبُ اَلنَّاسُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3154 - Aban narrated from Abu al-‘Abbas, meaning al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Malik, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdullah (as), \"Did the Messenger of Allah (swt) (peace be upon him and his family) declare Medina a sanctuary?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"Yes, he declared an area of a barid (about 22 kilometers) by a barid as a sanctuary, forbidding the cutting of its of its ʿIdhāhāʾ (trees).\"\nI then asked: \"What about its hunting?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"People do not lie.\""
        ]
      }
